1. Permission and scope

You may view and read this public repository for portfolio review. GitHub's
built-in viewing and forking features remain available. Before any other use
of the original RENA software and documentation (the "Software"), you must
contact Renato Pinto as described in section 3.

After that contact, and subject to all conditions below, you may run, copy
and modify the Software free of charge for your own personal or internal
organizational use. You may share copies and adaptations free of charge,
provided you retain this license, preserve the author's copyright notice
and identify your changes. Each recipient must independently satisfy the
contact requirement before use; contact by a distributor does not cover
other users.

2. No sale or paid distribution

You must not sell, resell, rent, license for a fee or otherwise distribute
the Software or its adaptations for payment, including as part of a paid
software bundle. You must not offer the Software or its adaptations as a
paid hosted service or charge others for access to them. Contacting the
author does not grant permission for any of these activities.

Using the Software internally to operate your own rent-a-car business does
not, by itself, constitute selling the Software. Such use still requires
prior contact under section 3.

3. Contact before any use and notification of adaptations

Every individual or organization must contact Renato Pinto before running,
testing, evaluating, modifying, integrating, deploying or otherwise using
the Software beyond the repository viewing and forking permitted in section
1. This applies to personal, educational, internal and business use, with or
without modifications. Rent-a-car companies and contractors acting for them
must identify the company and describe its intended use before deployment.

Identify yourself or your organization and explain the intended use and any
planned adaptations through the contact channel below. This is a prior
contact requirement; waiting for approval is not required. Own use remains
free of charge after contact, subject to this license. Contact never waives
the prohibition on sale or paid distribution.

Anyone making an adaptation must inform Renato Pinto of the changes and their
intended use. Provide a brief description when making the adaptation and
notify the author again of subsequent adaptations. A GitHub issue or pull
request describing the adaptation satisfies this requirement. You do not
need to submit your modified source code or wait for approval.

4. Contact channel

Submit a usage or adaptation notice at:
https://github.com/quebranozes/rena-rent-a-car/issues/new?template=usage-notification.md

An alternative contact channel expressly provided by the author may also be
used. Keep public notices free of confidential business or personal records.

5. Attribution and third-party material

Retain the attribution "RENA by Renato Pinto (@quebranozes)" in distributed
copies and associated documentation. Do not imply the author endorses an
adaptation. Third-party components remain under their own licenses, listed
in THIRD_PARTY.md; these conditions do not override those licenses.

